hived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-09-06T17:19:34Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T21:20:08Z","closed_at":"2026-09-08T20:55:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.6.3.\nGodot 4.7.2.\nGodot 4.8 dev4.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev4 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor (1600x900 @ 60.00 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated Radeon RX 560 Series (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21912.14) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-4570 CPU @ 3.20GHz (4 threads) - 15.93 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I connect two animations to a blend2 node, the animations behave unpredictably and are out of sync with each other:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e171a707-a395-45d9-82f3-467f494ff4ce\n\nThe first animation moves the cube along the X axis, the second along the Z axis.\n\nThe problem goes away after restarting the project.\nBut when I start moving the blending strength slider, the animation seems to break and stutter again.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82c31cdc-408d-4a05-8127-9ba019453442\n\n**Sync** does not change the situation after the changes described in the error report have been applied.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open MRP.\n2. In AnimationTree, detach one of the animations and reattach it, or change the blending strength in blend2.\n3. The animation is out of sync and jerky.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[anim-tree.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31884198/anim-tree.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuse